# Scenario diag-ctrl-psg-nokey (plan 05-11, D-24, V-08): outcome timeout, exit 11, detail budget. The
# same cartridge as diag-ctrl-psg-pass with no input line: both ports read idle (FF), the poll loop
# stores one value per port and never reaches eight port 0 values, so the guest is still polling,
# its end marker unwritten, when the run-to bound is reached first (deterministic machine time,
# never wall time). The contrast with the pass scenario shows that controller input, not time,
# changes guest state.
# expect-detail: budget step=1 line=15 expected=halted got=target
ivss 1
id diag-ctrl-psg-nokey
profile intv-2609-ntsc-family-p1
content exec boot-stub
content grom zero-grom
content cart diag-ctrl-psg-1.ivsc
capture psglog
run-to 12000 ticks stop halted
assert halted == yes
